WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:11.516
there were two mice, Tony and Rick.

2
00:00:12.277 --> 00:00:13.277
They were cousins.

3
00:00:13.597 --> 00:00:17.459
When they were young, they lived together in the country.

4
00:00:18.999 --> 00:00:24.922
When they grew up, Rick moved to the city, but Tony stayed in the country.

5
00:00:25.882 --> 00:00:29.844
Tony loved the country, but Rick did not.

6
00:00:30.908 --> 00:00:32.669
"I love the country.

7
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.872
It's clean, it's quiet, and it's safe."

8
00:00:38.633 --> 00:00:41.655
One day Tony got a letter from Rick.

9
00:00:43.116 --> 00:00:46.479
"Rick is coming to visit me here in the country.

10
00:00:47.199 --> 00:00:50.021
This is so fantastic!

11
00:00:50.781 --> 00:00:53.944
I can't wait to see my cousin again."

12
00:00:53.964 --> 00:00:55.885
"Hello, Tony."

13
00:00:55.905 --> 00:00:57.726
"Hello, Rick.

14
00:00:58.366 --> 00:01:00.268
I missed you very much."

15
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:02.521
"I have missed you too, cousin."

16
00:01:04.241 --> 00:01:07.202
Now Tony had a very humble house.

17
00:01:07.862 --> 00:01:10.503
He lived in the back of an old barn.

18
00:01:11.383 --> 00:01:15.464
He also had little to eat, just a few crumbs.

19
00:01:16.404 --> 00:01:22.386
But he had worked very hard to prepare a nice dinner for his cousin Rick.

20
00:01:24.227 --> 00:01:28.548
"I have made you a very fancy dinner, Rick.

21
00:01:29.368 --> 00:01:34.729
Tonight we will eat some very nice carrots and cabbage."

22
00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:45.272
After dinner was finished, Rick smiled at Tony and said, "Tony, my country cousin, you are very poor.

23
00:01:45.732 --> 00:01:49.774
Your house is nothing but a barn, and you have almost nothing to eat.

24
00:01:51.354 --> 00:01:55.315
In the city I eat cheese, meat, and bread every night."

25
00:01:56.055 --> 00:01:58.436
Tony looked very surprised.

26
00:01:58.976 --> 00:02:04.779
He said with envy, "Cheese, meat, and bread every night?"

27
00:02:04.799 --> 00:02:06.840
"Oh yes.

28
00:02:07.441 --> 00:02:09.762
And I live in a beautiful, warm house.

29
00:02:10.322 --> 00:02:12.404
Your barn is cold and dark."

30
00:02:13.244 --> 00:02:16.426
Tony became very envious of the city mouse.

31
00:02:17.066 --> 00:02:20.088
He decided to leave his poor country house.

32
00:02:20.108 --> 00:02:23.370
"I want to live in the city.

33
00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:27.372
I want to live in a beautiful, warm house."

34
00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.401
"Come with me to the city.

35
00:02:29.841 --> 00:02:31.322
You can have all you want."

36
00:02:32.603 --> 00:02:36.205
So the next day, the two mice went to the city.

37
00:02:36.985 --> 00:02:39.306
But Tony didn't like the city.

38
00:02:39.326 --> 00:02:43.389
"The city is very dirty and noisy.

39
00:02:44.109 --> 00:02:45.570
Where are the birds?

40
00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.971
I can't hear them sing."

41
00:02:47.991 --> 00:02:50.172
"We don't have any birds."

42
00:02:51.013 --> 00:02:52.694
"Where are the frogs?

43
00:02:53.354 --> 00:02:55.075
I can't hear them croak."

44
00:02:55.815 --> 00:02:56.796
"No frogs here."

45
00:02:57.848 --> 00:02:59.248
"Where is the sun?

46
00:02:59.889 --> 00:03:01.469
I don't see it shine."

47
00:03:02.089 --> 00:03:03.730
"It's behind the tall buildings.

48
00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.270
Would you like to see my beautiful house?"

49
00:03:07.171 --> 00:03:07.951
"Of course."

50
00:03:09.531 --> 00:03:11.972
So off they went to Rick's house.

51
00:03:13.332 --> 00:03:18.114
The house was indeed beautiful and very large.

52
00:03:18.794 --> 00:03:22.075
When Tony saw the house, he was amazed.

53
00:03:22.995 --> 00:03:25.356
"What a wonderful house!"

54
00:03:25.976 --> 00:03:29.577
"Shh! You must be very quiet or the woman will see you.

55
00:03:30.237 --> 00:03:32.978
If the woman sees you, she will kill you."

56
00:03:34.038 --> 00:03:36.159
Tony was very afraid.

57
00:03:36.719 --> 00:03:39.019
He did not want the woman to see him.

58
00:03:39.039 --> 00:03:40.540
"Let's eat!"

59
00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:47.922
When Tony saw the wonderful pile of food scraps, his eyes almost popped out of his head.

60
00:03:47.942 --> 00:03:50.763
"Look at this food.

61
00:03:51.663 --> 00:03:55.764
I have never seen so much food in my life."

62
00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:59.341
Tony began to eat the wonderful food.

63
00:04:00.342 --> 00:04:02.062
But then, bam!

64
00:04:03.163 --> 00:04:06.705
A large broom came crashing down in front of him.

65
00:04:06.725 --> 00:04:08.345
"Run, cousin!

66
00:04:08.745 --> 00:04:12.267
Run! If the woman catches you, she will kill you."

67
00:04:13.488 --> 00:04:16.989
Tony ran and he ran and he ran.

68
00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:20.451
He ran all the way back to the country.

69
00:04:21.351 --> 00:04:23.172
He was very frightened.

70
00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:28.110
He did not stop running until he was safe in his barn.

71
00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:32.493
"I will never go back to the city.

72
00:04:33.393 --> 00:04:34.934
I love the country.

73
00:04:35.915 --> 00:04:37.035
I am safe here.

74
00:04:38.136 --> 00:04:40.217
It is clean and quiet.

75
00:04:41.297 --> 00:04:42.538
I love the birds.

76
00:04:43.419 --> 00:04:44.719
I love the frogs.

77
00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:46.820
I love the sun."

78
00:04:47.581 --> 00:04:51.183
Tony never ever left the country again.
